(5681680, 825105, 109796, '<td valign="top">Is that a car or a ghost of one? How''d you do that? I''m really hoping you didn''t break any rules, I like this photo a lot... I like the how the photo matches the theme with a dark privacy feel. 7/10</td>', 'Is that a car or a ghost of one? How''d you do that? I''m really hoping you didn''t break any rules, I like this photo a lot... I like the how the photo matches the theme with a dark privacy feel. 7/10', '2009-10-09 12:55:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681705, 826187, 92768, '<td valign="top">very cute!</td>', 'very cute!', '2009-10-09 13:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681746, 825298, 92545, '<td valign="top">I always love insect photos.  Having said that, I don''t really see him as a hidden treasure.  The contrast of the black on the yellow doesn''t make it seem very "hidden" to me. It seems that you nailed the focus right on the right part of the bee, though.  I''m sure I would have voted this higher on another challenge.</td>', 'I always love insect photos.  Having said that, I don''t really see him as a hidden treasure.  The contrast of the black on the yellow doesn''t make it seem very "hidden" to me. It seems that you nailed the focus right on the right part of the bee, though.  I''m sure I would have voted this higher on another challenge.', '2009-10-09 14:12:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681756, 826117, 92545, '<td valign="top">I think this works well as a "hidden challenge" (unlike most of the shots I''ve looked through).  It seems that the focus might be on the front of the shell rather than the pearl, though.  I think if you had nailed the focus a bit better, this could have been good.  As a side note, I might have experimented with different crops to see if a more horizontal version of this might have worked better.  Having said that, you may have already done this and decided on this one.  I know that I get comments about cropping, and I''ve already tried many different crops and they didn''t work for one reason or another.  :-)</td>', 'I think this works well as a "hidden challenge" (unlike most of the shots I''ve looked through).  It seems that the focus might be on the front of the shell rather than the pearl, though.  I think if you had nailed the focus a bit better, this could have been good.  As a side note, I might have experimented with different crops to see if a more horizontal version of this might have worked better.  Having said that, you may have already done this and decided on this one.  I know that I get comments about cropping, and I''ve already tried many different crops and they didn''t work for one reason or another.  :-)', '2009-10-09 14:16:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681757, 826211, 92545, '<td valign="top">I think including this in the "hidden treasures" challenge is a bit of a stretch.  :-)  Other than that, this is a bit too much of a candid snapshot in my opinion.  You might have been able to increase the drama with a different angle or a different crop.  I could see a shallow depth of field shot that really drew attention to the "treasure" rather than the person.  A bit of brightness/contrast work in post processing could have made this pop a bit more as well.  4</td>', 'I think including this in the "hidden treasures" challenge is a bit of a stretch.  :-)  Other than that, this is a bit too much of a candid snapshot in my opinion.  You might have been able to increase the drama with a different angle or a different crop.  I could see a shallow depth of field shot that really drew attention to the "treasure" rather than the person.  A bit of brightness/contrast work in post processing could have made this pop a bit more as well.  4', '2009-10-09 14:19:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681760, 826223, 92545, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure exactly what kind of score you were expecting on this one.  :-)  I think you''ll get a lot of low scores for the "ewwww" factor.  I think I have to agree too.  The idea of this as a "hidden treasure" is debatable at best.  In addition to the ewww factor, though, This could have used some better lighting, a sharper focus, and less noise.  I''m sure shooting bats isn''t easy due to the lighting conditions, but this could have used a bit more setup to make it better.  A wider, off-centered, crop could have helped too.</td>', 'I''m not sure exactly what kind of score you were expecting on this one.  :-)  I think you''ll get a lot of low scores for the "ewwww" factor.  I think I have to agree too.  The idea of this as a "hidden treasure" is debatable at best.  In addition to the ewww factor, though, This could have used some better lighting, a sharper focus, and less noise.  I''m sure shooting bats isn''t easy due to the lighting conditions, but this could have used a bit more setup to make it better.  A wider, off-centered, crop could have helped too.', '2009-10-09 14:22:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681762, 825760, 92545, '<td valign="top">I haven''t used the word "shoehorn" at all in my commenting, but I HAVE to throw it in here.  :-)  I think including this in the challenge is a stretch (at best).  In addition, I don''t really know what you were going for in this shot. The reflections seem a bit blurry and the noise level is pretty high.  Perhaps I''m just too ignorant to understand.  (a distinct possibility)  3</td>', 'I haven''t used the word "shoehorn" at all in my commenting, but I HAVE to throw it in here.  :-)  I think including this in the challenge is a stretch (at best).  In addition, I don''t really know what you were going for in this shot. The reflections seem a bit blurry and the noise level is pretty high.  Perhaps I''m just too ignorant to understand.  (a distinct possibility)  3', '2009-10-09 14:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681766, 825555, 92545, '<td valign="top">Ok, I get the "hidden treasure" in the shot, but the flat lighting really hurts this one.  It''s also pretty tough to make a washing machine interesting, although I''ve seen other mundane objects treated very well before.  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=747607" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=747607</a> <br/> <br/>Mainly, I think this could have used some better lighting and maybe some brightness/contrast work in post processing.</td>', 'Ok, I get the "hidden treasure" in the shot, but the flat lighting really hurts this one.  It''s also pretty tough to make a washing machine interesting, although I''ve seen other mundane objects treated very well before.  //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=747607  Mainly, I think this could have used some better lighting and maybe some brightness/contrast work in post processing.', '2009-10-09 14:27:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681767, 825414, 92545, '<td valign="top">I think it''s a stretch to call this a "hidden treasure".  The bright lighting also washed out slot of the detail in the white elements in the shot.  You might even notice that his forehead seamlessly blends into the background.  I''m doubt this could be remedied in post processing, but some exposure compensation in the original shot could have brought it down.  3</td>', 'I think it''s a stretch to call this a "hidden treasure".  The bright lighting also washed out slot of the detail in the white elements in the shot.  You might even notice that his forehead seamlessly blends into the background.  I''m doubt this could be remedied in post processing, but some exposure compensation in the original shot could have brought it down.  3', '2009-10-09 14:28:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681769, 826119, 92545, '<td valign="top">I guess this IS a "hidden treasure", but it''s a bit bland for my taste.  The lighting is pretty flat and the crop leaves some undesirably human collateral while removing part of the car that might have given it balance.  3</td>', 'I guess this IS a "hidden treasure", but it''s a bit bland for my taste.  The lighting is pretty flat and the crop leaves some undesirably human collateral while removing part of the car that might have given it balance.  3', '2009-10-09 14:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681774, 825337, 92545, '<td valign="top">I don''t see this as a "hidden treasure", so I''m not sure why it''s in this challenge.  In addition, the bird is a bit blurry.  I''m not sure if it''s cropped from a much larger image of if the focus missed or a faster shutter speed was in order, but it could have been much sharper.  3</td>', 'I don''t see this as a "hidden treasure", so I''m not sure why it''s in this challenge.  In addition, the bird is a bit blurry.  I''m not sure if it''s cropped from a much larger image of if the focus missed or a faster shutter speed was in order, but it could have been much sharper.  3', '2009-10-09 14:32:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681778, 825466, 92545, '<td valign="top">I don''t really see this meeting the challenge.  Also, the narrow depth of field makes it really hard to get any meaningful part of the spider in focus.  The only part of the spider that I see in focus is one of his legs.  Perhaps if you could have gotten more of the body in focus, it would have grabbed my attention more.  The background is a bit distracting as well.  Perhaps a slightly different angle would have removed a bit of the yellow.  3</td>', 'I don''t really see this meeting the challenge.  Also, the narrow depth of field makes it really hard to get any meaningful part of the spider in focus.  The only part of the spider that I see in focus is one of his legs.  Perhaps if you could have gotten more of the body in focus, it would have grabbed my attention more.  The background is a bit distracting as well.  Perhaps a slightly different angle would have removed a bit of the yellow.  3', '2009-10-09 14:33:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681781, 826156, 92545, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorites.  I think your photo matches the topic perfectly.  You captured this at the PERFECT time.  The sunlight on the trees above the dwellings makes them look like the yellow of aspens in the fall.</td>', 'This is one of my favorites.  I think your photo matches the topic perfectly.  You captured this at the PERFECT time.  The sunlight on the trees above the dwellings makes them look like the yellow of aspens in the fall.', '2009-10-09 14:35:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681782, 825296, 92545, '<td valign="top">I loved this.  Way to find a hidden treasure!!!  I just wish dpchallenge didn''t require such severe compression.  I would love to see this without the compression.</td>', 'I loved this.  Way to find a hidden treasure!!!  I just wish dpchallenge didn''t require such severe compression.  I would love to see this without the compression.', '2009-10-09 14:35:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681783, 826203, 92545, '<td valign="top">Truly creative.  It''s not my absolute favorite for this challenge, but it matches the topic well and I must say, I''ve never seen such a great photo of the inside of a peanut butter jar.</td>', 'Truly creative.  It''s not my absolute favorite for this challenge, but it matches the topic well and I must say, I''ve never seen such a great photo of the inside of a peanut butter jar.', '2009-10-09 14:35:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681784, 825091, 92545, '<td valign="top">I almost marked this down because it wasn''t "hidden", but it fits well enough for me.  I suppose it was hidden since it''s in a cabinet.  That picture is SO me.  Love it.</td>', 'I almost marked this down because it wasn''t "hidden", but it fits well enough for me.  I suppose it was hidden since it''s in a cabinet.  That picture is SO me.  Love it.', '2009-10-09 14:35:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681785, 825560, 92545, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo.  I wish it were a bit larger, but that''s not your fault.  Did you desaturate this a bit?  I''m not sure if I like it that way or not.  It caught my eye, but I always love to see greens pop in waterfall pics.  I still give it a solid 7.</td>', 'Lovely photo.  I wish it were a bit larger, but that''s not your fault.  Did you desaturate this a bit?  I''m not sure if I like it that way or not.  It caught my eye, but I always love to see greens pop in waterfall pics.  I still give it a solid 7.', '2009-10-09 14:35:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681786, 825907, 92545, '<td valign="top">This is a tough one.  I really like the photo.  You certainly did well with that lighting at hand.  It''s always tough to photograph a room like this when you have such bright highlights and such dark shadows.  If there were a candidate for an hdr treatment, this certainly would be it.  I know that''s not legal so I can''t fault you for it.  I give it a solid 7.</td>', 'This is a tough one.  I really like the photo.  You certainly did well with that lighting at hand.  It''s always tough to photograph a room like this when you have such bright highlights and such dark shadows.  If there were a candidate for an hdr treatment, this certainly would be it.  I know that''s not legal so I can''t fault you for it.  I give it a solid 7.', '2009-10-09 14:35:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681787, 825947, 92545, '<td valign="top">I originally rated this a 6, but I''m going to bump this up because I''ve been commenting on all my sixes, and I think this is better than that.  I think I originally rated it so low because I''m not sure how this fits in the challenge.  It didn''t hit the nail right on the head for me, but it''s such a beautiful photo, I''m bumping you up to a 7.</td>', 'I originally rated this a 6, but I''m going to bump this up because I''ve been commenting on all my sixes, and I think this is better than that.  I think I originally rated it so low because I''m not sure how this fits in the challenge.  It didn''t hit the nail right on the head for me, but it''s such a beautiful photo, I''m bumping you up to a 7.', '2009-10-09 14:35:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681788, 826086, 92545, '<td valign="top">I love the blues.  For such lackluster lighting, you did a great job.  It fits the challenge and is a solid photo.  I''m not sure if I''m crazy about the centered composition of the "hidden treasure", but I''m not sure if I would have composed it any other way myself.  :-)  I give it a solid 7.</td>', 'I love the blues.  For such lackluster lighting, you did a great job.  It fits the challenge and is a solid photo.  I''m not sure if I''m crazy about the centered composition of the "hidden treasure", but I''m not sure if I would have composed it any other way myself.  :-)  I give it a solid 7.', '2009-10-09 14:35:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681789, 826097, 92545, '<td valign="top">Matches the challenge, good focus.  Solid 7.</td>', 'Matches the challenge, good focus.  Solid 7.', '2009-10-09 14:35:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681790, 826228, 92545, '<td valign="top">I really like your idea and the execution was good.  Your lighting was much better than I could have done.  The only nagging thing is the distortion of the straight lines.  On the third row down, you have a "dp" together.  I was really hoping to find "challenge" in there as well.  Solid 7</td>', 'I really like your idea and the execution was good.  Your lighting was much better than I could have done.  The only nagging thing is the distortion of the straight lines.  On the third row down, you have a "dp" together.  I was really hoping to find "challenge" in there as well.  Solid 7', '2009-10-09 14:35:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681791, 826217, 92545, '<td valign="top">I''m not really sure exactly what I''m looking at.  I like it, but I wonder if it''s too tight a crop.  Frankly, I''m not sure if it is or not.  With the image dimension requirements, you might have completely lost the subject.  I still like the photo.  7</td>', 'I''m not really sure exactly what I''m looking at.  I like it, but I wonder if it''s too tight a crop.  Frankly, I''m not sure if it is or not.  With the image dimension requirements, you might have completely lost the subject.  I still like the photo.  7', '2009-10-09 14:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681792, 825879, 92545, '<td valign="top">An interesting choice.  Placing it on the map really enhanced the photo even though the two aren''t really tied together.  Off topic, but that really looks like a piranha plant from Super Mario to me.  7</td>', 'An interesting choice.  Placing it on the map really enhanced the photo even though the two aren''t really tied together.  Off topic, but that really looks like a piranha plant from Super Mario to me.  7', '2009-10-09 14:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681793, 826148, 92545, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure why I''m not rating this higher.  I like the composition, the lighting is great, and the colors are beautiful.  There''s something that i can''t quite put my finger on that''s nagging me about this picture.  Is it the focus?  I can''t put my finger on it.  I still like the photo.  6</td>', 'I''m not sure why I''m not rating this higher.  I like the composition, the lighting is great, and the colors are beautiful.  There''s something that i can''t quite put my finger on that''s nagging me about this picture.  Is it the focus?  I can''t put my finger on it.  I still like the photo.  6', '2009-10-09 14:35:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681794, 825068, 92545, '<td valign="top">I think I would have liked a little more contrast here.  (not necessarily in the composition, but maybe in the editing)  It''s a nice photo, but nothing stands out to me.  6</td>', 'I think I would have liked a little more contrast here.  (not necessarily in the composition, but maybe in the editing)  It''s a nice photo, but nothing stands out to me.  6', '2009-10-09 14:35:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681795, 825980, 92545, '<td valign="top">A great photo, but I think the placement in this challenge is a stretch.  I would have ranked it higher otherwise.  6  I really like the reds on the pillow.</td>', 'A great photo, but I think the placement in this challenge is a stretch.  I would have ranked it higher otherwise.  6  I really like the reds on the pillow.', '2009-10-09 14:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681796, 825653, 92545, '<td valign="top">I like the composition and the subject.  It works well having both the blooming rose and the bud.  I wish there were a bit more contrast between the rose and the background.  It all seems a bit "orangy" (sorry, I know it''s not a word) to me.  Maybe a cooler color temperature would have helped (although I know you may have been going for the warmness)  I had this as a 5, but after looking at it in depth, I''m moving it to a 6.  If it fit the challenge a bit better, I probably would have given it a higher score.</td>', 'I like the composition and the subject.  It works well having both the blooming rose and the bud.  I wish there were a bit more contrast between the rose and the background.  It all seems a bit "orangy" (sorry, I know it''s not a word) to me.  Maybe a cooler color temperature would have helped (although I know you may have been going for the warmness)  I had this as a 5, but after looking at it in depth, I''m moving it to a 6.  If it fit the challenge a bit better, I probably would have given it a higher score.', '2009-10-09 14:36:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681800, 825765, 92545, '<td valign="top">The sharpness of this is very good.  You were definitely shooting for this challenge in particular.  :-)  I just wish it were a little bit brighter in the nest. I''m sure that was impossible with the natural light at the time you took this, but I think it would have balanced the photo better.  I think a slightly wider crop would have been interesting as well.  6</td>', 'The sharpness of this is very good.  You were definitely shooting for this challenge in particular.  :-)  I just wish it were a little bit brighter in the nest. I''m sure that was impossible with the natural light at the time you took this, but I think it would have balanced the photo better.  I think a slightly wider crop would have been interesting as well.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681801, 826205, 92545, '<td valign="top">I''m sure this was a challenge to catch.  I''ve tried some aquarium photography and almost always been disappointed, usually because of the high ISO noise on my Rebel XTI.  I think it''s a nice capture, but my eye is immediately drawn to his back because there''s not enough light on his face.  Not that you can do anything about the lighting, but if you had caught him looking up, I think I would have preferred it.  Also, I find the tie to this challenge tenuous at best.  Keep up the good work, though.  I''m very impressed with the sharpness.  6</td>', 'I''m sure this was a challenge to catch.  I''ve tried some aquarium photography and almost always been disappointed, usually because of the high ISO noise on my Rebel XTI.  I think it''s a nice capture, but my eye is immediately drawn to his back because there''s not enough light on his face.  Not that you can do anything about the lighting, but if you had caught him looking up, I think I would have preferred it.  Also, I find the tie to this challenge tenuous at best.  Keep up the good work, though.  I''m very impressed with the sharpness.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681803, 826154, 92545, '<td valign="top">Aren''t moments like this glorious?  At first I wasn''t sure I liked the composition, but I''ve decided I like the symmetry left to right.  I might have tried to crop out the trees, though.  I don''t think they add anything. Also, some color adjustments might have made this ''pop'' a bit more.  6</td>', 'Aren''t moments like this glorious?  At first I wasn''t sure I liked the composition, but I''ve decided I like the symmetry left to right.  I might have tried to crop out the trees, though.  I don''t think they add anything. Also, some color adjustments might have made this ''pop'' a bit more.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681804, 826206, 92545, '<td valign="top">Great photo.  I think it''s a stretch on this particular challenge.  If it were somewhere else, I would definitely give it a higher score.  I love the composition and this particular shot has so much action to it.  Sorry to give you a 6.  Great shot, wrong challenge.</td>', 'Great photo.  I think it''s a stretch on this particular challenge.  If it were somewhere else, I would definitely give it a higher score.  I love the composition and this particular shot has so much action to it.  Sorry to give you a 6.  Great shot, wrong challenge.', '2009-10-09 14:38:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681805, 826204, 92545, '<td valign="top">A lovely photo, but it''s not a "hidden treasure" to me.  Also, I think it could have used some contrast adjustment to make it pop a bit more.  6</td>', 'A lovely photo, but it''s not a "hidden treasure" to me.  Also, I think it could have used some contrast adjustment to make it pop a bit more.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681806, 825105, 92545, '<td valign="top">I love this photo for some reason.  Did you zoom during the exposure for this effect?  There''s an otherworldly quality to it.  I just don''t see it as a "hidden treasure".  I would otherwise given this a higher score.  6</td>', 'I love this photo for some reason.  Did you zoom during the exposure for this effect?  There''s an otherworldly quality to it.  I just don''t see it as a "hidden treasure".  I would otherwise given this a higher score.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681807, 826046, 92545, '<td valign="top">An interesting photo.  It just seems to lack detail on the subject.  Were you trying to focus on the very tip? because I think it fell slightly further down.  Believe me, this is a major critique of my own macro photography.  I still love the colors.  If the focus were better, I would probably bump this up 2 points.  I gave this a five, but it''s better than all of my other five photos...  6</td>', 'An interesting photo.  It just seems to lack detail on the subject.  Were you trying to focus on the very tip? because I think it fell slightly further down.  Believe me, this is a major critique of my own macro photography.  I still love the colors.  If the focus were better, I would probably bump this up 2 points.  I gave this a five, but it''s better than all of my other five photos...  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681808, 825437, 92545, '<td valign="top">There''s something pleasing about this.  I''m not sure it matches the challenge, though.  6</td>', 'There''s something pleasing about this.  I''m not sure it matches the challenge, though.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681809, 826136, 92545, '<td valign="top">an interesting shot for this challenge, but the lighting doesn''t really "wow" me.  6</td>', 'an interesting shot for this challenge, but the lighting doesn''t really "wow" me.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681810, 825267, 92545, '<td valign="top">I love the color of the fly.  I definitely wish the dimensions didn''t have to be so small.  I''m sure that his eyes are bursting with detail.  My only problem is that some of the photo is just washed out.  I know that if you darkened it, you would probably lose some detail, but the brightness just doesn''t quite work for me.  I still give it a 6.</td>', 'I love the color of the fly.  I definitely wish the dimensions didn''t have to be so small.  I''m sure that his eyes are bursting with detail.  My only problem is that some of the photo is just washed out.  I know that if you darkened it, you would probably lose some detail, but the brightness just doesn''t quite work for me.  I still give it a 6.', '2009-10-09 14:38:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681811, 825846, 92545, '<td valign="top">I really haven''t had a chance to photograph rainbows yet, so I can''t really critique with any knowledge of the subject, but....  the central portions of the rainbow or blown out just a bit.  Just enough to leave me unsatisfied.  I wonder if a tighter crop and some post processing could have helped a bit.  What a wonderful moment to capture, though.  This really reminds me of where I grew up, Alamogordo, New Mexico. 6</td>', 'I really haven''t had a chance to photograph rainbows yet, so I can''t really critique with any knowledge of the subject, but....  the central portions of the rainbow or blown out just a bit.  Just enough to leave me unsatisfied.  I wonder if a tighter crop and some post processing could have helped a bit.  What a wonderful moment to capture, though.  This really reminds me of where I grew up, Alamogordo, New Mexico. 6', '2009-10-09 14:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681812, 825869, 92545, '<td valign="top">What a wonderfully beautiful place.  I''m not sure if this really goes with the challenge, though.  Also, with the miniscule dimensions required by dpchallenge, I can''t really tell if the focus is spot on or not.  Right now it''s making me want to reach for some glasses, but that could just be the image size.  6</td>', 'What a wonderfully beautiful place.  I''m not sure if this really goes with the challenge, though.  Also, with the miniscule dimensions required by dpchallenge, I can''t really tell if the focus is spot on or not.  Right now it''s making me want to reach for some glasses, but that could just be the image size.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681813, 826163, 92545, '<td valign="top">I like the authentic "film feel" to this.  The composition is nice as well, although I wonder if a slightly higher or lower angle would have brought out the lighthouse better.  6</td>', 'I like the authentic "film feel" to this.  The composition is nice as well, although I wonder if a slightly higher or lower angle would have brought out the lighthouse better.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681814, 825610, 92545, '<td valign="top">I don''t see this as a hidden treasure.  I give it a 6  Otherwise, it''s a great shot.  I''m wondering what kind of flash you used for this.  The reflections are a little bit blown from the flash.  I know I don''t have the equipment to remedy any of that.  It''s a better job that I could do with the same subject.  Having said that, you should check out <br/><a href="//nocroppingzone.blogspot.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">nocroppingzone.blogspot.com</a> <br/>Somewhere in there, you''ll find the equipment he uses and I know he has some diffusers for his specialty macro flash.  Interesting stuff and AMAZING macro insect photography.</td>', 'I don''t see this as a hidden treasure.  I give it a 6  Otherwise, it''s a great shot.  I''m wondering what kind of flash you used for this.  The reflections are a little bit blown from the flash.  I know I don''t have the equipment to remedy any of that.  It''s a better job that I could do with the same subject.  Having said that, you should check out nocroppingzone.blogspot.com Somewhere in there, you''ll find the equipment he uses and I know he has some diffusers for his specialty macro flash.  Interesting stuff and AMAZING macro insect photography.', '2009-10-09 14:38:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681815, 825092, 92545, '<td valign="top">This is a very literal take on the challenge.  I like it, but the quite swirl coming out of the chest detracts from the image.  I''m not sure what caused it or if the cause could have been removed.  Otherwise, I think the focus should have been on the chest rather than the waterfall.  (If my eyes deceive me and the lid of the chest is not out of the water and the chest is completely underwater, ignore my comment and call me an idiot because I know that a clear focus is impossible with the shutter speed used.)  I give it a 6.</td>', 'This is a very literal take on the challenge.  I like it, but the quite swirl coming out of the chest detracts from the image.  I''m not sure what caused it or if the cause could have been removed.  Otherwise, I think the focus should have been on the chest rather than the waterfall.  (If my eyes deceive me and the lid of the chest is not out of the water and the chest is completely underwater, ignore my comment and call me an idiot because I know that a clear focus is impossible with the shutter speed used.)  I give it a 6.', '2009-10-09 14:38:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681816, 826072, 92545, '<td valign="top">Wow, this could have worked in both challenges.  :-)  I suppose that hidden treasures had fewer entries, though.  I love the idea.  Reminds me a bit of pulp fiction, but I think you executed it well. I think I would have liked a bit more brightness or some more saturation to the color, though.  Perhaps a curves adjustment to increase brightness and contrast?  Overall I like the idea.  6</td>', 'Wow, this could have worked in both challenges.  :-)  I suppose that hidden treasures had fewer entries, though.  I love the idea.  Reminds me a bit of pulp fiction, but I think you executed it well. I think I would have liked a bit more brightness or some more saturation to the color, though.  Perhaps a curves adjustment to increase brightness and contrast?  Overall I like the idea.  6', '2009-10-09 14:38:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681817, 826133, 92545, '<td valign="top">You certainly did a great job of making this look authentic.  I don''t think it matches the challenge very well, though.  Also, it kind of looks like the kid is on his cellphone.  I like the look on his face.  I''m sure you had a lot of fun shooting this.</td>', 'You certainly did a great job of making this look authentic.  I don''t think it matches the challenge very well, though.  Also, it kind of looks like the kid is on his cellphone.  I like the look on his face.  I''m sure you had a lot of fun shooting this.', '2009-10-09 14:38:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681818, 825788, 92545, '<td valign="top">Wow, I just realized how many mirrors were in this picture.  At first glance, I didn''t notice any mirrors.  I''m not sure about the fit in this challenge, but it''s definitely a photo-worthy spot.  It seems to me that it could be a bit sharper.  (I think this about alot of my own photos)  I give it a 5.</td>', 'Wow, I just realized how many mirrors were in this picture.  At first glance, I didn''t notice any mirrors.  I''m not sure about the fit in this challenge, but it''s definitely a photo-worthy spot.  It seems to me that it could be a bit sharper.  (I think this about alot of my own photos)  I give it a 5.', '2009-10-09 14:38:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681819, 825311, 92545, '<td valign="top">I don''t really get this shot.  It doesn''t really fit the challenge to me.  Also, the composition doesn''t excite me.  Perhaps if she were a bit off-center, it would pop more.  Her skin is blown out a bit as well.  You were obviously shooting in difficult lighting conditions.  I don''t know that I could remedy any of that, but that''s what I see when I look at this photo.  5</td>', 'I don''t really get this shot.  It doesn''t really fit the challenge to me.  Also, the composition doesn''t excite me.  Perhaps if she were a bit off-center, it would pop more.  Her skin is blown out a bit as well.  You were obviously shooting in difficult lighting conditions.  I don''t know that I could remedy any of that, but that''s what I see when I look at this photo.  5', '2009-10-09 14:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681820, 825896, 92545, '<td valign="top">I love the quality of this image, but I''m not crazy about the crop and the border.  I also don''t see the hidden treasure.  I would love to give this a higher score, but I''m stuck on a 5.  (my apologies, I know the quality of this image is much greater than a 5, I just don''t get it in this challenge)</td>', 'I love the quality of this image, but I''m not crazy about the crop and the border.  I also don''t see the hidden treasure.  I would love to give this a higher score, but I''m stuck on a 5.  (my apologies, I know the quality of this image is much greater than a 5, I just don''t get it in this challenge)', '2009-10-09 14:39:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681821, 826126, 92545, '<td valign="top">Definitely a literal interpretation of the challenge.  :-)  Quirky idea.  With such a shallow depth of field, I think I would have tried to nail the focus on the skeleton himself to really draw attention to him.  Right not, it looks to me as if the focus is dead on the chest.  5  I like the bright colors.</td>', 'Definitely a literal interpretation of the challenge.  :-)  Quirky idea.  With such a shallow depth of field, I think I would have tried to nail the focus on the skeleton himself to really draw attention to him.  Right not, it looks to me as if the focus is dead on the chest.  5  I like the bright colors.', '2009-10-09 14:39:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681822, 826035, 92545, '<td valign="top">I don''t get this for this challenge.  Also, I think a slightly tighter crop would have eliminated the tiny bit of grass I see in the bottom right-hand corner.  I always like shots like this, though.  I had a chance to shoot a (rather boring) sunset through some tall grass and it really made it pop.  5</td>', 'I don''t get this for this challenge.  Also, I think a slightly tighter crop would have eliminated the tiny bit of grass I see in the bottom right-hand corner.  I always like shots like this, though.  I had a chance to shoot a (rather boring) sunset through some tall grass and it really made it pop.  5', '2009-10-09 14:39:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681823, 825745, 92545, '<td valign="top">I love the colors, but the tilted edge of the aquarium puts me off a bit.  Perhaps a straighter shot would have helped.  My only other complaint is the same complaint I have of my similar shots... the noisiness of the photo.  I''m sure it''s just a limitation of the camera, but it''s still a complaint.  :-)  5</td>', 'I love the colors, but the tilted edge of the aquarium puts me off a bit.  Perhaps a straighter shot would have helped.  My only other complaint is the same complaint I have of my similar shots... the noisiness of the photo.  I''m sure it''s just a limitation of the camera, but it''s still a complaint.  :-)  5', '2009-10-09 14:39:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681824, 825799, 92545, '<td valign="top">Technically, I love the shot.  I don''t catch it''s inclusion in this challenge.  If it fit the challenge better, I''d give it a higher score for sure.  5</td>', 'Technically, I love the shot.  I don''t catch it''s inclusion in this challenge.  If it fit the challenge better, I''d give it a higher score for sure.  5', '2009-10-09 14:39:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681830, 825972, 92545, '<td valign="top">Argh.  I typed a long comment in here just to have dpchallenge glitch on me and lose it all.  Well, I''ll try to recreate my comments.  :-)<br/> <br/>I''m not sure I see this as a "hidden treasure"  The hidden part of it just isn''t there for me.  It must be a gem of a place to photograph, though.  I think I would have preferred the sharpest focus to be on the church, rather than the fence.  Overall the lighting seems a bit drab to me.  I think some brightness/contrast work might have helped this pop a bit more.  Also, I''m not sure what caused it... (usually I associate it with hdr), but there is a slight halo around the church and the tree.  Was that from post processing?  Overall, I like the angle, but I would definitely go back and try to catch it with some more dramatic lighting.  5</td>', 'Argh.  I typed a long comment in here just to have dpchallenge glitch on me and lose it all.  Well, I''ll try to recreate my comments.  :-) I''m not sure I see this as a "hidden treasure"  The hidden part of it just isn''t there for me.  It must be a gem of a place to photograph, though.  I think I would have preferred the sharpest focus to be on the church, rather than the fence.  Overall the lighting seems a bit drab to me.  I think some brightness/contrast work might have helped this pop a bit more.  Also, I''m not sure what caused it... (usually I associate it with hdr), but there is a slight halo around the church and the tree.  Was that from post processing?  Overall, I like the angle, but I would definitely go back and try to catch it with some more dramatic lighting.  5', '2009-10-09 14:43:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681926, 826154, 110654, '<td valign="top">Absolutley perfect</td>', 'Absolutley perfect', '2009-10-09 16:17:02.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5681927, 826171, 70270, '<td valign="top">My immediate reaction: Doesn''t do much for me, either as a standalone photo or insofar as meeting the challenge.  But a nice close up of her eyes, and I''m sure she is a treasure to you (though not really a hidden one).   Probably a 6 in the Eyes challenge, but just a 5 here.</td>', 'My immediate reaction: Doesn''t do much for me, either as a standalone photo or insofar as meeting the challenge.  But a nice close up of her eyes, and I''m sure she is a treasure to you (though not really a hidden one).   Probably a 6 in the Eyes challenge, but just a 5 here.', '2009-10-09 16:18:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681928, 825437, 104009, '<td valign="top">i rated this a 7 on my second pass, the first time i couldn''t see how it''s a hidden treasure, but on reflection i see it now.  well done.</td>', 'i rated this a 7 on my second pass, the first time i couldn''t see how it''s a hidden treasure, but on reflection i see it now.  well done.', '2009-10-09 16:25:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681929, 826163, 104009, '<td valign="top">great shot nice use of b&amp;w and deep dof.  7</td>', 'great shot nice use of b&w and deep dof.  7', '2009-10-09 16:26:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681931, 825942, 104009, '<td valign="top">i LOVE this picture but can''t wrap my mind around the hidden treasure aspect of it.  6.</td>', 'i LOVE this picture but can''t wrap my mind around the hidden treasure aspect of it.  6.', '2009-10-09 16:26:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681933, 825907, 104009, '<td valign="top">can''t se ehow this is a hidden treasure when it''s so dilapidated? love the lighting and the setup and the colors.  6.</td>', 'can''t se ehow this is a hidden treasure when it''s so dilapidated? love the lighting and the setup and the colors.  6.', '2009-10-09 16:27:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681934, 825765, 104009, '<td valign="top">great title and setup. nice colors and use of shallow dof.  8</td>', 'great title and setup. nice colors and use of shallow dof.  8', '2009-10-09 16:28:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681935, 824777, 104009, '<td valign="top">not very hidden, and not exaclt a treasure i suppose.  but i love the subject and the contrast.  6.</td>', 'not very hidden, and not exaclt a treasure i suppose.  but i love the subject and the contrast.  6.', '2009-10-09 16:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681936, 825914, 104009, '<td valign="top">i don''t know exactly what the hands are holding so i can''t deem it "treasure" worthy, BUT i like the picture. 6</td>', 'i don''t know exactly what the hands are holding so i can''t deem it "treasure" worthy, BUT i like the picture. 6', '2009-10-09 16:29:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681938, 825972, 104009, '<td valign="top">GREAT shot but no title and not sure how it''s a hidden treasure?  6</td>', 'GREAT shot but no title and not sure how it''s a hidden treasure?  6', '2009-10-09 16:30:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681939, 826175, 104009, '<td valign="top">can''t see the "hidden treasure" aspect even on my second pass, but my original scoring was way too harsh i moved it form 4 to 6 because it''s a beautiful picture.</td>', 'can''t see the "hidden treasure" aspect even on my second pass, but my original scoring was way too harsh i moved it form 4 to 6 because it''s a beautiful picture.', '2009-10-09 16:31:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681973, 826211, 104009, '<td valign="top">i''m confused by the title and the subject....does the title refer to the girl, or to what she''s holding?nice picture but i can''t rationalize how it meets the challenge.  5</td>', 'i''m confused by the title and the subject....does the title refer to the girl, or to what she''s holding?nice picture but i can''t rationalize how it meets the challenge.  5', '2009-10-09 17:00:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681975, 825799, 104009, '<td valign="top">great shallow dof picture but dont see how it meets the challenge. 5</td>', 'great shallow dof picture but dont see how it meets the challenge. 5', '2009-10-09 17:00:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681977, 825760, 104009, '<td valign="top">not sure if the title is full of typoes or if it''s something else i don''t understand, but i don''t get how it meets the challenge.  4.</td>', 'not sure if the title is full of typoes or if it''s something else i don''t understand, but i don''t get how it meets the challenge.  4.', '2009-10-09 17:01:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5681980, 825810, 104009, '<td valign="top">beautiful colors.  not sure how it meets the criteria for the challenge though and very unbalanced shot.   5.</td>', 'beautiful colors.  not sure how it meets the criteria for the challenge though and very unbalanced shot.   5.', '2009-10-09 17:03:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682012, 826097, 70270, '<td valign="top">Angle of the shot hurts this and loses interest.  Get down lower and shoot across his nose, not down at it.  Too snapshottish to me, and not much tie to the challenge.  Sorry.  4<br/> <br/>ETA:  I''ve looked again and I think I see what you''re going for, with his tongue reaching into a crack.  Hard to see against that background, and still doesn''t conjure up a "treasure" to me, but bumping you up to a 5 because its closer than I initially gave you credit for.</td>', 'Angle of the shot hurts this and loses interest.  Get down lower and shoot across his nose, not down at it.  Too snapshottish to me, and not much tie to the challenge.  Sorry.  4 ETA:  I''ve looked again and I think I see what you''re going for, with his tongue reaching into a crack.  Hard to see against that background, and still doesn''t conjure up a "treasure" to me, but bumping you up to a 5 because its closer than I initially gave you credit for.', '2009-10-09 17:49:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682067, 825942, 48657, '<td valign="top">well done on a challenging capture. balancing detail in the carriage and noise was a problem for sure but you seem to have pulled it off.</td>', 'well done on a challenging capture. balancing detail in the carriage and noise was a problem for sure but you seem to have pulled it off.', '2009-10-09 19:02:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682069, 825105, 48657, '<td valign="top">Nice capture, DOF is excellent, not sure about the reflection on the subject, would have been cleaner if it could have been taken without. In my opinion.</td>', 'Nice capture, DOF is excellent, not sure about the reflection on the subject, would have been cleaner if it could have been taken without. In my opinion.', '2009-10-09 19:07:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682070, 826061, 48657, '<td valign="top">who cares about the one oclock sun, nice use of it. Nice back light and colors</td>', 'who cares about the one oclock sun, nice use of it. Nice back light and colors', '2009-10-09 19:09:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682075, 826206, 48657, '<td valign="top">Good job on this sharp action image, I like the crop, but I would have straightened out the grass or even tilted it the other way slightly to give the horse even more angle.</td>', 'Good job on this sharp action image, I like the crop, but I would have straightened out the grass or even tilted it the other way slightly to give the horse even more angle.', '2009-10-09 19:15:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682087, 825879, 48657, '<td valign="top">Nice what a simple composition and good DOF can create. Nice contrast and texture.</td>', 'Nice what a simple composition and good DOF can create. Nice contrast and texture.', '2009-10-09 19:27:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682121, 825918, 77196, '<td valign="top">This looks like a beautiful spot. To me, the shot looks very over processed. I''d also suggest cropping a bit closer on the lower edge. This would still include the path, but would make the shot feel a bit wider angle.</td>', 'This looks like a beautiful spot. To me, the shot looks very over processed. I''d also suggest cropping a bit closer on the lower edge. This would still include the path, but would make the shot feel a bit wider angle.', '2009-10-09 20:32:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682122, 825091, 77196, '<td valign="top">Great expression.</td>', 'Great expression.', '2009-10-09 20:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682131, 826163, 77196, '<td valign="top">When you''re doing a centered image, being off just a little is very noticeable. To me, this looks like the camera position wants to be just a bit to the right (photographer''s perspective). Somehow I''m also bothered by the horizon bisecting the house. A lower perspective would have put the house in the sky (or maybe just sitting on the horizon). I like the strong sense of visual deception created by the angles of the sides of the jetty, leading your eye to the light house.</td>', 'When you''re doing a centered image, being off just a little is very noticeable. To me, this looks like the camera position wants to be just a bit to the right (photographer''s perspective). Somehow I''m also bothered by the horizon bisecting the house. A lower perspective would have put the house in the sky (or maybe just sitting on the horizon). I like the strong sense of visual deception created by the angles of the sides of the jetty, leading your eye to the light house.', '2009-10-09 20:42:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682137, 826211, 77196, '<td valign="top">There are lots of things I like about this shot. Love the bright pink shirt &amp; matching lipstick. Nice indeterminate expression - makes me want to know more about what she is thinking. However, the orange earrings and red steps / bookcase clash with the pink. Also, if the photog was able to take about 1 step to the left, the fence post would have disappeared behind the cache, the steps / bookcase would have been out of frame, and her head would have hidden the white blob above her left ear.</td>', 'There are lots of things I like about this shot. Love the bright pink shirt & matching lipstick. Nice indeterminate expression - makes me want to know more about what she is thinking. However, the orange earrings and red steps / bookcase clash with the pink. Also, if the photog was able to take about 1 step to the left, the fence post would have disappeared behind the cache, the steps / bookcase would have been out of frame, and her head would have hidden the white blob above her left ear.', '2009-10-09 20:48:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682138, 825765, 77196, '<td valign="top">Great idea. Maybe a blue jay or raven''s nest - don''t they collect bright baubles to hide? The lighting and refractions of the gems are very nice.</td>', 'Great idea. Maybe a blue jay or raven''s nest - don''t they collect bright baubles to hide? The lighting and refractions of the gems are very nice.', '2009-10-09 20:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682144, 826156, 77196, '<td valign="top">Tough lighting - from dark in the canyon to the last rays of sunlight over lighting the trees on the top. Yet it is the same lighting that is absolutely gorgeous on the adobe buildings. I would suggest a much tighter crop on this - left side to just right of foreground rock; right to just left of 3rd large rock cropping, and top down to just above the rim rocks. I think that would leave enough of the shot to communicate cliff dwellings and remove a lot of distracting elements. Your shot has a lot of "bonus"es - the moon, the golden trees, the very nice blue sky, the line of the canyon leading back, to the left, and behind. IMO, none of these are strong enough to add to the shot. Instead the temptation is to include them, which dilutes the attention focal point of the picture.</td>', 'Tough lighting - from dark in the canyon to the last rays of sunlight over lighting the trees on the top. Yet it is the same lighting that is absolutely gorgeous on the adobe buildings. I would suggest a much tighter crop on this - left side to just right of foreground rock; right to just left of 3rd large rock cropping, and top down to just above the rim rocks. I think that would leave enough of the shot to communicate cliff dwellings and remove a lot of distracting elements. Your shot has a lot of "bonus"es - the moon, the golden trees, the very nice blue sky, the line of the canyon leading back, to the left, and behind. IMO, none of these are strong enough to add to the shot. Instead the temptation is to include them, which dilutes the attention focal point of the picture.', '2009-10-09 20:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682145, 825617, 77196, '<td valign="top">The lighting and detail on this is very, very nice. It draws you into its mystery and story. The glow in the upper window is an awesome touch.</td>', 'The lighting and detail on this is very, very nice. It draws you into its mystery and story. The glow in the upper window is an awesome touch.', '2009-10-09 21:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682146, 825466, 77196, '<td valign="top">Sorry - not a fan of blurry shots. To me, there is not enough in focus to catch your attention. The spider is the main object in the shot, and it is OOF. Only a very small part of the web looks to be in focus (probably the "silk" treasure), and then you have a large chartreuse blob in the upper left corner taking up about 1/3 of the shot. It does add color, but does not seem to serve an obvious purpose in your message.</td>', 'Sorry - not a fan of blurry shots. To me, there is not enough in focus to catch your attention. The spider is the main object in the shot, and it is OOF. Only a very small part of the web looks to be in focus (probably the "silk" treasure), and then you have a large chartreuse blob in the upper left corner taking up about 1/3 of the shot. It does add color, but does not seem to serve an obvious purpose in your message.', '2009-10-09 21:05:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5682150, 825907, 77196, '<td valign="top">Seems like I''ve seen this room before in another challenge. I love the blue peeling paint on the wall, the abandoned look of the lone desk. A bit too much dark on the left &amp; right sides, and there was probably no way to lose the (relatively) modern light fixture...</td>', 'Seems like I''ve seen this room before in another challenge. I love the blue peeling paint on the wall, the abandoned look of the lone desk. A bit too much dark on the left & right sides, and there was probably no way to lose the (relatively) modern light fixture...', '2009-10-09 21:07:05.000000', NULL, 1),
