(5686269, 826072, 93421, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon!  Great shot!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon!  Great shot!', '2009-10-14 01:40:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686325, 826097, 108580, '<td valign="top">Thanks commentators (4 of you found Waldo, the hidden ant) and voters!  I''m thinking 73 of the voters also spotted him. This challenge and the stats below tell me a lot about how DPC thinks and interprets them. I also realised that subjective/dubious challenges should result in a shot that almost needs to be in your face to do well.<br/> <br/>&lt;5 = 45 (I don''t think they got it)<br/>=5 = 77 (I think they did or didn''t get it and were being kind)<br/>&gt;5 = 73 (I think they got it)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-10-14 01:29:38.</i></td>', 'Thanks commentators (4 of you found Waldo, the hidden ant) and voters!  I''m thinking 73 of the voters also spotted him. This challenge and the stats below tell me a lot about how DPC thinks and interprets them. I also realised that subjective/dubious challenges should result in a shot that almost needs to be in your face to do well. <5 = 45 (I don''t think they got it)=5 = 77 (I think they did or didn''t get it and were being kind)>5 = 73 (I think they got it)', '2009-10-14 02:03:39.000000', '2009-10-14 02:29:38.000000', 0),
(5686329, 826097, 108580, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EstimatedEyes:</b></div><hr/><i> Angle of the shot hurts this and loses interest.  Get down lower and shoot across his nose, not down at it.  Too snapshottish to me, and not much tie to the challenge.  Sorry.  4<br/> <br/>ETA:  I''ve looked again and I think I see what you''re going for, with his tongue reaching into a crack.  Hard to see against that background, and still doesn''t conjure up a "treasure" to me, but bumping you up to a 5 because its closer than I initially gave you credit for. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thx for commenting and ETA''ing. His tongue however is not poking out. I would have cropped this shot better if not for the ant...who is actually dangling on a spiders web!</td>', 'Originally posted by EstimatedEyes: Angle of the shot hurts this and loses interest.  Get down lower and shoot across his nose, not down at it.  Too snapshottish to me, and not much tie to the challenge.  Sorry.  4 ETA:  I''ve looked again and I think I see what you''re going for, with his tongue reaching into a crack.  Hard to see against that background, and still doesn''t conjure up a "treasure" to me, but bumping you up to a 5 because its closer than I initially gave you credit for.   Thx for commenting and ETA''ing. His tongue however is not poking out. I would have cropped this shot better if not for the ant...who is actually dangling on a spiders web!', '2009-10-14 02:05:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686336, 825092, 108580, '<td valign="top">Wd, only 9 I gave out. Pity about the typo :) Maybe SC will let you "fix" it...<br/> <br/>Edit: They did!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-10-15 04:30:16.</i></td>', 'Wd, only 9 I gave out. Pity about the typo :) Maybe SC will let you "fix" it... Edit: They did!', '2009-10-14 02:09:39.000000', '2009-10-15 05:30:16.000000', 0),
(5686362, 825092, 102534, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your votes, comments and encouragement ... a Blue Ribbon! Brilliant!! Personally, I think this is one of my best ever photos. <br/>@mark082: the swirl is actually a pearl necklace, but as it was submerged and the shot was taken on a slow shutter, came out blurred by the current and bubbles on the surface. The chest was completely submerged, so the open wooden chest lid is floating close to the surface but moving due to the current.<br/>@Magnum_za: Yes, the darkness had me questioning myself, but the lighter versions just don''t do it for me. The environment was left as i found it except for perhaps a few stray coins that I couldn''t reach on the stream bed. I have asked the SC if they can correct my lousy spelling .... fingers crossed :)</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your votes, comments and encouragement ... a Blue Ribbon! Brilliant!! Personally, I think this is one of my best ever photos. @mark082: the swirl is actually a pearl necklace, but as it was submerged and the shot was taken on a slow shutter, came out blurred by the current and bubbles on the surface. The chest was completely submerged, so the open wooden chest lid is floating close to the surface but moving due to the current.@Magnum_za: Yes, the darkness had me questioning myself, but the lighter versions just don''t do it for me. The environment was left as i found it except for perhaps a few stray coins that I couldn''t reach on the stream bed. I have asked the SC if they can correct my lousy spelling .... fingers crossed :)', '2009-10-14 02:40:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686366, 826072, 102534, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, very creative shot</td>', 'Congratulations, very creative shot', '2009-10-14 02:42:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686368, 826203, 102534, '<td valign="top">Makes me chuckle every time i look at this. Congratulations on the ribbon and a tip of my hat to your creativity.</td>', 'Makes me chuckle every time i look at this. Congratulations on the ribbon and a tip of my hat to your creativity.', '2009-10-14 02:42:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686443, 826072, 52549, '<td valign="top">Connor, your first ribbon!! What a beautiful image, it''s been a pleasure watching your progress since you joined dpc. Great work and congratulations!</td>', 'Connor, your first ribbon!! What a beautiful image, it''s been a pleasure watching your progress since you joined dpc. Great work and congratulations!', '2009-10-14 03:20:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686446, 826203, 52549, '<td valign="top">It''s clever and creative - and it makes me smile every time I look at it ;-) Many congrats, Joe.</td>', 'It''s clever and creative - and it makes me smile every time I look at it ;-) Many congrats, Joe.', '2009-10-14 03:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686465, 826203, 45559, '<td valign="top">A ribbon with this score?!... get outta'' here. Congrats dude :P</td>', 'A ribbon with this score?!... get outta'' here. Congrats dude :P', '2009-10-14 03:38:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686467, 825092, 54398, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of the Goonies so much!! Great photo.</td>', 'This reminds me of the Goonies so much!! Great photo.', '2009-10-14 03:39:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686486, 826203, 45631, '<td valign="top">Love this.  Congrats on your ribbon.</td>', 'Love this.  Congrats on your ribbon.', '2009-10-14 03:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686510, 825092, 52549, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your blue. Wonderful image.</td>', 'Congrats on your blue. Wonderful image.', '2009-10-14 04:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686517, 826203, 79955, '<td valign="top">Congrats Joe !!!!! this is super &amp; original !!! love it</td>', 'Congrats Joe !!!!! this is super & original !!! love it', '2009-10-14 05:09:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686521, 825310, 79955, '<td valign="top">WOW!!! This is super cool and a super shot!! Congrats on the ribbon</td>', 'WOW!!! This is super cool and a super shot!! Congrats on the ribbon', '2009-10-14 05:15:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686524, 825091, 45631, '<td valign="top">Love this.  Well done and a great idea.</td>', 'Love this.  Well done and a great idea.', '2009-10-14 05:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686525, 825092, 110994, '<td valign="top">Love anything Nikon, but if you need a critique, the shot is well composed and stunning but too surreal.  It looks like, but not implying, that you worked it photoshop.  It has the "photo contest look."  You know?  I like it, it''s obviously great but too surreal for my taste.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Love anything Nikon, but if you need a critique, the shot is well composed and stunning but too surreal.  It looks like, but not implying, that you worked it photoshop.  It has the "photo contest look."  You know?  I like it, it''s obviously great but too surreal for my taste. ', '2009-10-14 05:27:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686539, 826046, 82127, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your critiques ;) !</td>', 'Thank you all for your critiques ;) !', '2009-10-14 06:18:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5686547, 826005, 94235, '<td valign="top">Lots of non surfers out there who wouldn''t have understood the message that an uncrowded surf break is a hidden treasure to most surfers. <br/>I''ll have remember to be more literal next time!</td>', 'Lots of non surfers out there who wouldn''t have understood the message that an uncrowded surf break is a hidden treasure to most surfers. I''ll have remember to be more literal next time!', '2009-10-14 06:35:46.000000', NULL, 0);
