(5691397, 825092, 106447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AllAccess:</b></div><hr/><i> Love anything Nikon, but if you need a critique, the shot is well composed and stunning but too surreal.  It looks like, but not implying, that you worked it photoshop.  It has the "photo contest look."  You know?  I like it, it''s obviously great but too surreal for my taste. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Whether it was shot with a Nikon, Canon, Sigma, whatever...What does that have to do with his entry?<br/>Are you implying Nikon shots are automatically superior? I would beg to disagree, and so would many others.</td>', 'Originally posted by AllAccess: Love anything Nikon, but if you need a critique, the shot is well composed and stunning but too surreal.  It looks like, but not implying, that you worked it photoshop.  It has the "photo contest look."  You know?  I like it, it''s obviously great but too surreal for my taste.   Whether it was shot with a Nikon, Canon, Sigma, whatever...What does that have to do with his entry?Are you implying Nikon shots are automatically superior? I would beg to disagree, and so would many others.', '2009-10-18 18:33:43.000000', NULL, 0),
